/-! # Connectivity development

This entry point exports the native PSPACE bounds for point and whole-space
semialgebraic connectivity, together with the supporting geometric and
computational development and its alternative constructions.

`NativeConnectivityPSPACE` contains the unconditional endpoints. They include
singleton validation for endpoint formulas and rejection of malformed inputs.
The constructive proof uses finite sign refinements, accessible frontier
covers, and polynomial-space graph reachability. The report's explicit roadmap
output and motion-planning interfaces are separate results.

Only the public import frontier is listed here: each omitted direct import is
already exported transitively by a retained module.
-/
